 ### SLM Phase Delay Modeling
-A model for the phase delay $\phi_\lambda$ imparted by an LCoS SLM, accounting for wavelength dispersion [S3]. The phase delay is $\phi_\lambda = \frac{2\pi d}{\lambda} n(s, \lambda)$, where $d$ is the LC layer thickness, $n(s, \lambda)$ is the refractive index controlled by digital input $s$ and dependent on $\lambda$ [S3]. Quantization errors increase with larger phase ranges, requiring at least 6 bits of granularity per $2\pi$ range to maintain PSNR/SSIM [S3].
